 "notes": "DRAFT (Claude, 2026-09-24) - needs human review. Traced on frames/cleanplate_pose_A.png (per-pixel median of 60 settled frames from sample_001 f1000+ and sample_002), registered to sample_001 f3400 within ~1 px. Scene: divided avenue from the upper-left to the right edge with a raised median; a one-way OUTBOUND leg at the bottom-left under the diagonal zebra; camera high on the SW corner. SB = near side of the median, flows down-right to the stop line; NB = far side, enters from the right edge and flows to the upper-left. CAMERA POSE: this geometry fits sample_001 after ~frame 900 and all of sample_002. sample_001 frames 0-~900 sit ~22 px off; sample_004 ~15-60 px off; sample_003 ~55-150 px off (shift -130,+77, scale 1.014, rot -1 deg) - a static zones.json is NOT valid there without per-video registration. DIRECTIONS: every lane arrow is along its painted lines with the sign taken from optical flow measured over 40 one-second windows. MANOEUVRES: no painted lane arrows are visible, so permitted_manoeuvres is empty (unknown) everywhere; flow suggests SB1_flare carries the right turn into the bottom-left leg. NB approach: no stop line visible and its signal faces away from the camera, so red_light/stop_line cannot be judged for NB. SIGNAL: TL_median_nose is the only readable head (red top, amber middle, green bottom; ROI encloses all three lamps in pose A; green reads confirmed by SB traffic crossing the stop line 84% (sample_001) / 69% (sample_002) of the time; red lamp lights only 3-11 px so src/thresholds.py min_lit_pixels=12 returns UNKNOWN for most red phases - a threshold calibration issue, not the ROI); the overhead gantry heads show only backplates; the 2-lamp head on the camera-corner mast is unused (purpose unknown). NB left-turners cross the SB through stream into the bottom-left leg; that conflict area deliberately has no lane. PARKING: the left parking bay and the right corner plaza are outside the carriageway; buses dwell at the NB bus stop (Q_NB_busstop). The service road beyond the far sidewalk at the very top is excluded."
}